{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"length","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\"kind\":\"final\",\"decision\":\"answer\",\"answer\":16,\"","reasoning_content":"We have a problem: 12 variables (0-11). 8 XOR equations. Need count of assignments satisfying all equations. We can solve linear system over GF(2). Count = 2^(n - rank). Need rank. Let's compute rank manually.\n\nEquations list:\n\n1) x3 + x7 + x9 = 1\n2) x0 + x3 = 1\n3) x3 + x7 + x8 = 0\n4) x8 + x11 = 1\n5) x0 + x3 + x6 + x8 = 0\n6) x0 + x2 + x6 + x7 = 0\n7) x3 + x7 + x9 = 1 (duplicate of 1)\n8) x3 + x8 = 0\n\nWe can ignore duplicate 7. Also note equation 8: x3 + x8 = 0 => x3 = x8.\n\nEquation 3: x3 + x7 + x8 = 0. Substitute x3=x8 gives x8 + x7 + x8 = x7 = 0 => x7 = 0.\n\nEquation 1: x3 + x7 + x9 = 1. With x7=0, gives x3 + x9 = 1 => x9 = x3 + 1.\n\nEquation 2: x0 + x3 = 1 => x0 = x3 + 1.\n\nEquation 4: x8 + x11 = 1. Since x8=x3, gives x3 + x11 = 1 => x11 = x3 + 1.\n\nEquation 5: x0 + x3 + x6 + x8 = 0. Substitute x0=x3+1, x8=x3: (x3+1)+x3+x6+x3 = 0. Compute: x3+1 + x3 + x6 + x3 = combine x3 terms: x3 + x3 + x3 = x3 (since 3 mod 2 =1). So we have x3 + 1 + x6 = 0 => x6 = x3 + 1.\n\nEquation 6: x0 + x2 + x6 + x7 = 0. Substitute x0=x3+1, x6=x3+1, x7=0: (x3+1)+x2+(x3+1)+0 = 0. Simplify: x3+1 + x2 + x3+1 = (x3+x3)+(1+1)+x2 = 0+0+x2 = x2. So x2 = 0.\n\nThus all variables expressed in terms of x3. Variables:\n\nx3 = free variable t ∈ {0,1}\nx8 = t\nx7 = 0\nx9 = t+1\nx0 = t+1\nx11 = t+1\nx6 = t+1\nx2 = 0\nRemaining variables: x1, x4, x5 are unconstrained? They don't appear in any equation. So they are free as well.\n\nCount free variables: x3, x1, x4, x5. That's 4 free variables. So number of solutions = 2^4 = 16.\n\nCheck consistency: All equations satisfied for any t. Good.\n\nThus answer 16.\n\nWe need to provide final JSON with decision answer 16, evidence receipt-1, confidence maybe 1.0, status SUPPORTED, reason short.\n\nLet's produce."}}],"created":1790938139,"model":"C:\\Users\\d2j3\\Documents\\Cod